sequenceDiagram
    participant Operator as Operator<br/>(kubectl exec)
    participant K8sAPI as Kubernetes API<br/>443/TCP HTTPS
    participant PreflightHTTP as Preflight HTTP Server<br/>8000/TCP HTTP
    participant vLLM as vLLM Process
    participant GPU as NVIDIA GPU<br/>nvidia-smi
    participant PodA as Pod A<br/>(Server)
    participant PodB as Pod B<br/>(Client)
    participant Creator as NIXL Creator Agent
    participant Peer as NIXL Peer Agent<br/>5555/TCP ZMQ

    Note over Operator,vLLM: Flow 1: Preflight Check (Pause Mode)
    PreflightHTTP->>GPU: Collect topology (nvidia-smi, lscpu, lspci)
    GPU-->>PreflightHTTP: GPU topology, NVLink status
    PreflightHTTP->>PreflightHTTP: Start HTTP server on port 8000
    Operator->>PreflightHTTP: GET /info (kubectl exec port-forward)
    PreflightHTTP-->>Operator: System diagnostics JSON
    Operator->>PreflightHTTP: GET /exit
    PreflightHTTP-->>Operator: 200 OK (shutting down)
    PreflightHTTP->>vLLM: Exit → vLLM starts (via && chain)

    Note over Operator,Peer: Flow 2: Networking Tests
    Operator->>K8sAPI: Pod discovery (label selector)
    K8sAPI-->>Operator: Pod list (llm-d.ai/model)
    Operator->>PodA: kubectl exec (start perftest server)
    PodA->>PodA: ib_write_bw listening on 18515/TCP
    Operator->>PodB: kubectl exec (start perftest client)
    PodB->>PodA: RDMA bandwidth test (18515/TCP)
    PodA-->>PodB: Bandwidth results
    Operator->>Operator: Collect results, generate matplotlib plots

    Note over Creator,Peer: Flow 3: NIXL Benchmark
    Peer->>Peer: Bind ZMQ PAIR socket (5555/TCP)
    Peer->>GPU: Allocate GPU tensor dataset (VRAM)
    Creator->>Peer: Connect ZMQ (5555/TCP)
    Creator->>GPU: Allocate GPU tensor dataset (VRAM)
    Creator->>Peer: Exchange metadata (ZMQ)
    Peer-->>Creator: Metadata response (ZMQ)
    Creator->>Peer: NIXL data transfer (UCX RDMA/TCP, dynamic port)
    Peer-->>Creator: Transfer completion notification (ZMQ)
    Creator->>Creator: Calculate throughput metrics
